{%- comment -%}
  The free delivery threshold, formatted, from the one setting that defines it.

  Every "free delivery over X" line on the site renders this, so the number can
  only ever be changed in one place: Brand > Free delivery threshold. The cart
  page and the bag drawer compute their progress bars from the same setting.

  at_least: 1 guards the cart page, which divides by the threshold to size its
  progress bar — a merchant typing 0 would otherwise divide by zero.

  round is not cosmetic. A decimal threshold makes `times: 100` a float: 54.99 * 100
  is 5498.999999999999, and the live Shopify money filter rounds that to the whole
  euro, so the site read "orders over €55" while the policy and the discount both
  said €54.99. The preview harness's money filter does not do this, so it rendered
  €54.99 and the bug reached the live theme green. round makes the cents integral
  before any money filter sees them. cart-drawer and main-cart do the same for the
  same reason.

  Usage: {% render 'free-delivery-amount' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{{- settings.free_shipping_threshold | at_least: 1 | times: 100 | round | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
